WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.317
"Microbiome Manipulation
with Oligomannate for Dementia"

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.680
In 2020 a remarkable
case report was published

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.560
entitled “Rapid improvement in
Alzheimer's disease symptoms

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:19.040
following fecal microbiota
transplantation: a case report.”

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.160
The FDA allows the use of fecal
transplants for the treatment

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.880
of recalcitrant infections
of a bad bug known as C diff.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.040
Serendipitous improvements
following such transplants

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.720
across a range of conditions
have been reported,

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.440
including autism, baldness,
and multiple sclerosis.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.840
The dementia report involved

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.320
an 82-year-old man with
a five-year history

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.160
of gradually declining
memory and cognition.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.440
His Mini-Mental State
Examination score

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.320
was 20 (out of 30), indicating
mild cognitive impairment.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.040
But two months after receiving a
fecal transplant from his wife

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.280
his score was 26, which is
considered normal cognition.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.680
By month six post-transplant,

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.600
the patient achieved a near
perfect score of 29,

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.240
and he also reported
a marked improvement

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.440
in mood, social interaction,
and expressiveness.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.200
The potential role
of gut flora in Alzheimer's

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.880
is not completely
out of left field.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.240
Butyrate, which is
what our good gut bugs

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.200
produce when we eat fiber,

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.760
is absorbed from our colon
into our bloodstream

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.680
and can cross
the blood-brain barrier

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:29.120
and improve the memory
function of mice and rats.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:32.840
In people, the microbiomes
of Alzheimer's patients

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.800
have been found to have
fewer good bugs-

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.320
butyrate-producing bugs-

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.160
and more bad bugs-
pro-inflammatory bugs.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.960
One reason this
isn't just dismissed

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:46.680
as a simple consequence of
poorer (lower fiber) diets

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.320
is that mice
transplanted with stool

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.880
from an Alzheimer's patient
perform significantly worse

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.040
on cognitive tasks than
those fed fecal samples

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.920
from a non-demented individual.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.440
Could it be that fecal
transplants actually help?

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:05.040
We'll find out soon, as a
randomized, double-blind,

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.240
placebo-controlled trial
of fecal transplants

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:11.040
for Alzheimer's disease
is currently underway.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.760
There have been
about two dozen studies

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.800
of prebiotics, probiotics,

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.560
and fermented
foods for cognition.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:21.000
Most reported improvements
in certain specific tasks,

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.400
but the findings were
inconsistent such that, overall,

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.200
there was no significant
improvement in global cognition,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.200
nor in any single
cognitive domain.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.960
Of course, differences in dosing
and formulations make it hard

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.440
to draw conclusions from such
heterogeneous data points.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.520
There was a randomized
double-blind

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.600
placebo-controlled
trial published

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:43.400
that purported to show a
significant improvement

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.960
in Mini-Mental
State Exam scores,

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.720
but the validity of the data

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.200
was later called into question.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.080
Similar concerns
haunt oligomannate,

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.240
a prebiotic conditionally
approved to treat

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:59.760
mild-to-moderate Alzheimer's
disease in China in 2019.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.600
Traditional Japanese
eating patterns

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.640
have been associated with
better cognitive function

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:07.480
in the elderly
and lower risk of dementia.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.360
That was evidently the
inspiration to try oligomannate,

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.120
a prebiotic derived from
a type of brown seaweed,

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.120
on a mouse model
of Alzheimer's disease.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.640
Cognition improved in the mice,

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.920
but a subsequent 24-week human
trial in Alzheimer's patients

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.680
failed to offer
a significant benefit.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:27.840
Not to be discouraged,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.600
the Shanghai Green Valley
Pharmaceutical Company,

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.160
the developers of oligomannate,

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:34.720
funded another human trial,

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.040
a 36-week multicenter,
randomized, double-blind,

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.400
placebo-controlled trial
of more than 800 patients

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.200
with mild-to-moderate
Alzheimer's dementia.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.480
Significant improvements in
cognition were noted

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.240
starting within
four weeks in those

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:50.440
randomized to oligomannate
compared to placebo.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.880
Based on that trial,

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:54.520
it went on sale in China
in December 2019

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.640
for about $500 a month.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.760
Currently, oligomannate is not
marketed outside of China,

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.320
but a similar phase 3
clinical trial is underway

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.840
in North America with trial
completion expected in 2026.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.280
A safety analysis found

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.560
that the overall incidence
of adverse reactions

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.280
did not differ significantly

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.560
between those getting
the active and placebo groups.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.880
Tempering enthusiasm
is the shady history

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:23.520
of Shanghai Green Valley
Pharmaceutical Company,

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.880
accused of a "whirlpool
of &amp; bribery and fraud"

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.240
for illegally marketing supposed
anti-cancer miracle drugs.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:34.600
A leading Chinese academic
suggested oligomannate could

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:39.560
"become the largest fraud case
in China in the 21st century."

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.040
The lead developer
of oligomannate

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.840
joined hundreds of other
Chinese researchers

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:48.040
who have been accused
of data falsification,

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.720
though a Chinese Ministry
of Science and Technology

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.400
investigation
concluded that only

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:59.560
a "small amount of misused
pictures were found."

